[Git Workflow Rules]
Always run `git branch` to verify the current branch before modifying files.
NEVER push, commit, or write code directly on the `main` branch.
All new work must be isolated in a dedicated branch (e.g., feature/task-name).

[Operational Protocol]
1. Step-by-step Verification: Process exactly one task at a time. Stop and request explicit user permission before proceeding to the next task.
2. Pre-task Clearance: Before any coding begins, check the branch. If on `main`, halt and ask the user for a new branch name to checkout.
3. Mandatory Notification: Upon completing ANY task or milestone, YOU MUST trigger the Telegram notification script (mcp-telegram.mjs) or an inline HTTP call to the Telegram API to alert the user that the task is finished, without exception.
